# REST Action Input Validation

## Always Use `Validate()` on REST Endpoints

Every REST endpoint in `setup-*-api.ts` must be wrapped with `Validate()` to enforce schema validation on incoming requests. This applies to URL params, query params, and request bodies.

```typescript
// ✅ Good - Validate wraps the action
'/files/:letter/:path/stream': Authorize()(
  Validate({ schema: mediaApiSchema, schemaName: 'StreamFileEndpoint' })(StreamAction),
),

// ❌ Bad - no Validate, raw input reaches the action
'/files/:letter/:path/master.m3u8': Authorize()(HlsMasterAction),
```

## Validate User-Controlled Params Before System Calls

Even with `Validate()`, action handlers that pass user input to system processes (FFmpeg, file system, shell) must explicitly validate critical parameters:

```typescript
// ✅ Good - explicit bounds checking before FFmpeg
const segmentIndex = parseInt(index, 10)
if (isNaN(segmentIndex) || segmentIndex < 0) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid segment index', 400)
}

if (from < 0 || to <= from) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid time range', 400)
}

const VALID_MODES: PlaybackMode[] = ['direct-play', 'remux', 'direct-stream', 'transcode']
if (!VALID_MODES.includes(mode)) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid playback mode', 400)
}

// ❌ Bad - unvalidated parseInt passed to FFmpeg args
const segmentIndex = parseInt(index, 10) // NaN or negative goes through
ffmpegArgs.push('-ss', String(from))      // negative from goes through
```

## Path Traversal Prevention

When constructing file paths from user input, always validate against directory traversal:

```typescript
// ✅ Good - path traversal check
const rel = relative(physicalParent, subtitlePath)
if (rel.startsWith('..') || resolve(subtitlePath) !== subtitlePath) {
  throw new RequestError('Invalid path', 400)
}
```
